  "question": {
    "text": "For one mole of an ideal gas, which of these statements must be true?<br />(a) Internal energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and enthalpy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>)</mo></math> each depends&nbsp;on temperature.<br />(b) Compressibility factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>&nbsp;is not equal to 1<br />(c) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math><br />(d) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>dU</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub><mi>dT</mi></math> for any process",
    "image": null
  },
